WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:04.765
Modelfiles help turn model setup into repeatable operational configuration.

00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:07.200
Instead of relying on undocumented manual choices,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.250
a Modelfile can describe a base model and the settings that shape how an internal model

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.260
variant behaves.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.310
That may include parameters, templates, system messages, adapters,

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:19.345
and licensing or source notes that help operators understand what they are running.

00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:22.440
Controlled variants are useful because different teams and workflows often need different

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:22.930
defaults.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:26.020
A support workflow may need a different tone, context window,

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.560
or response style than a developer assistant or a lab experiment.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.720
Without documented variants,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.060
teams can end up with several machines that appear to run the same model but behave

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.185
differently because someone changed a prompt,

00:00:36.185 --> 00:00:37.985
template, or runtime option locally.

00:00:37.985 --> 00:00:41.655
System messages and templates should be treated as operational configuration.

00:00:41.655 --> 00:00:45.400
They can affect user experience, safety expectations, support outcomes,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.640
and evaluation results.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.930
When those settings are used for shared workflows, they should be named, reviewed,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:51.250
versioned, and documented.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.590
A short note about why a setting exists can prevent confusion later.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:59.040
Repeatable configuration reduces drift between developer machines and shared environments.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.740
It also makes troubleshooting easier.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.160
If a model variant changed,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.865
teams can compare the Modelfile and related notes rather than guessing which manual step

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:06.610
was different.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:10.880
This is the difference between local experimentation and a supportable local AI service.
